A||||6||mrgone||what does the car look like with no headliner?||||1||
Z||000000||mrgone||06-17-2001||10:27 PM||||anyone have any pics?<BR>my head liner is [/b] really [/b] bothering me, i used an entire can of fabric adhesive on it, and a bunch of thumbtacks     nothing will keep it from drooping and being all ugly with its holes. its upsetting me.]<BR>if the roof underside looks like the trunk and hood underside and you dont really notice its missing it wont be so bad without one<P>no t tops or sunroof in my car btw||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||06-17-2001||10:40 PM||||Sorry, I have no pics but had my headliner out for a couple weeks while I recovered it a couple years ago.  Just the steel space frame with an opening in the middle which is just the plastic roof panel.  The space frame is black and the roof panel will have overspray on it of whatever color your car is.  <P>You may not want to totally remove your headliner either.  I found it made the car a LOT hotter inside without it.  The headliner fiberglass acts as insulation against the sun beating on the roof.  I was very happy to get it back into the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||06-17-2001||10:41 PM||||Take it out and recover it with NEW fabric (at most $20)||||reg||1
Z||000003||prtzlboy||06-17-2001||10:51 PM||||Check out the red GT in these pics, there should be a good pic.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/003274.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/003274.html</A> <P>This car now belongs to me btw   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  If it still had the sunvisors I wouldn't even notice that the headliner was missing.<p>[This message has been edited by prtzlboy (edited 06-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||06-17-2001||11:14 PM||||If you don't want to recover it you can varnish or coat it with 'glass resin.  It's kind of a pebbly finish anyway.  Then spray it the colour of your choice.<BR>Gary||||reg||8
Z||000005||Tigger||06-18-2001||12:53 AM||||I need to recover my headliner again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I'd say keep it.  I've drove my Fiero for a couple weeks without the headliner at one time.  Matter of fact I've drove it without door panels, and probably half of the interior out before.<P>Anyway, it gets kinda noisy on the highway.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||06-18-2001||01:59 AM||||I really like the look of it covered in vinyl. Just an idea.||||reg||1
